window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"message-your-dot\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dot\">给 dot 发消息</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>无论使用哪种已连接的联系方式，你联系的都是同一个 dot。切换渠道不会重置它的记忆。Slack 和 Teams 对话只显示在相应渠道中交换的消息，不会同步其他渠道的全部消息；不过，dot 可以利用这些对话中的相关上下文。若要与他人分享私人对话中的信息，它会先确认你是否允许。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=context-and-memory\">上下文与记忆</a>。</p> <p>打开 dot 的个人资料并选择 <strong>添加（Add）</strong>，即可查看并连接你可用的联系方式。应用和电脑需要单独连接，才能供 dot 在工作中使用。</p> <p><a id=\"chatgpt-and-voice\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT 与语音</h2> <p>你可以在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中创建 dot、给它发消息或打电话。移动网页版暂不支持。</p> <p>要给 dot 打电话，请打开与它的对话并选择电话按钮。在桌面应用中，也可以在它的个人资料中选择 <strong>通话（Call）</strong>。你可以通过语音说明请求、澄清决定或询问进度；通话时也能输入消息。dot 也可以通过消息向你汇报进度或提问。结束通话只会结束语音对话，已分派的工作仍可继续。dot 主动发起的电话计划在正式推出后提供。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：与 dot 进行语音通话的示例；旁边的聊天消息正在准备产品发布评审，并梳理尚待决定的事项。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"slack\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"slack-and-teams\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack-teams\">Slack 和 Teams</h2> <p>你可以通过 Slack 和 Microsoft Teams 给 dot 发消息。在 dot 的个人资料中连接相应联系方式即可。在 Slack 中，你可以给它发私信，也可以将它添加到某个频道，然后在讨论串中提及它。</p> <p>在 Slack 中，dot 默认只回应你。你可以要求它与其他人互动；它分享信息或采取行动时，仍受现有权限和安全措施约束。在频道中回复前，dot 可以先私信你，询问哪些内容可以分享。</p> <p>告诉 dot 不同类型的更新应该发送到哪里。例如，让它在 ChatGPT 中汇报日常进度，需要作决定时再通过 Slack 联系你。</p> <p>如需监控，请明确指定要检查哪些频道、关注什么内容，以及何时通知你。让 dot 确认已设置的重复任务。仅将 dot 添加到频道，并不会自动建立监控日程。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Slack 私信和回复讨论串示例：Alex 转发了一份发布计划。第二天早上，dot 提醒日程存在风险，Alex 则在讨论串中查看后续跟进的草稿。</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"ios-widgets-and-shortcuts\">iOS 小组件和快捷指令</h2> <p>在 iPhone 主屏幕上打开你的 dot，或使用 Apple 的 <strong>Shortcuts（快捷指令）</strong>选择如何开始对话。请使用最新版 ChatGPT iOS 应用，并登录你设置 dot 时所用的账户。该功能正随 ChatGPT iOS 版 1.2026.279 分批推出，且需要<a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">访问 dot 的资格</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"add-the-your-dot-widget\">添加 Your dot 小组件</h3> <blockquote> <p>插图：小尺寸的 Your dot 主屏幕小组件，显示 Alfred 的黄色角色和名称；快捷按钮处于隐藏状态。</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Your dot</strong> 小组件会在较小尺寸的主屏幕组件中显示 dot 的名称和外观。</p> <ol> <li>长按主屏幕上的空白区域，依次选择 <strong>Edit（编辑）</strong> &gt; <strong>Add Widget（添加小组件）</strong>。</li> <li>找到 <strong>ChatGPT</strong>，选择 <strong>Your dot</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Add Widget（添加小组件）</strong>。</li> <li>放置小组件后，选择 <strong>Done（完成）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>轻点 dot 即可打开对应对话，并直接进入消息输入框。例如，开完会后可打开它，把会议决定补充到你们正在协作的工作中。</p> <p>若要添加消息和通话按钮，请长按小组件，选择 <strong>Edit Widget（编辑小组件）</strong>，然后启用 <strong>Show shortcut buttons（显示快捷按钮）</strong>。此设置默认关闭。消息按钮会打开输入框；当你可以使用通话时会显示电话按钮，可用来发起通话或返回正在进行的通话。</p> <p>如果小组件提示你登录或设置 dot，请打开 ChatGPT 并完成相应步骤。仅添加小组件，不会让原本没有 dot 使用权限的账户自动获得访问权限。</p> <h3 id=\"create-an-apple-shortcut\">创建 Apple 快捷指令</h3> <p>ChatGPT 提供一个 <strong>Open your dot</strong> 操作，并有三种 <strong>Mode（模式）</strong>可选：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>模式</th> <th>作用</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>Messaging（消息）</strong></td> <td>打开 dot 对话以输入文字消息。这是默认模式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Dictation（听写）</strong></td> <td>开始语音转文字输入，为 dot 撰写消息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Call（通话）</strong></td> <td>开始实时语音对话，或返回正在进行的通话。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <ol> <li>打开 Apple 的 <strong>Shortcuts（快捷指令）</strong>应用并新建一个快捷指令。</li> <li>添加操作，搜索 <strong>Open your dot</strong>，然后选择 ChatGPT 操作。</li> <li>选择你的 dot，再选择一种 <strong>Mode（模式）</strong>。</li> <li>为快捷指令命名并保存，然后运行它，即可按所选模式打开 ChatGPT。</li> </ol> <p>例如，可保存一个名为“和我的 dot 通话”的快捷指令，并选择 <strong>Call（通话）</strong>模式，以口述方式查看进展。也可使用 <strong>Dictation（听写）</strong>快速口述一条消息。通话进行期间不能使用听写。</p> <p>在带有操作按钮的 iPhone 上，打开 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> &gt; <strong>Action Button（操作按钮）</strong>，选择 <strong>Shortcut（快捷指令）</strong> &gt; <strong>Choose a Shortcut（选择快捷指令）</strong>，然后选中刚保存的快捷指令。也可以从 Apple 的快捷指令主屏幕小组件运行已保存的快捷指令。</p> <p>该操作会打开 ChatGPT，且需要通过身份验证。如果你切换账户后，已保存的快捷指令提示 dot 不再可用，请登录拥有该 dot 的账户。</p> <p><a id=\"texting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">短信</h2> <p>短信功能即将推出。</p> <aside>     2026-10-18  </aside>","en":"<h1 id=\"message-your-dot\">Message your dot</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>You reach the same dot through each connected contact method. Changing channels doesn’t reset its memory. Slack and Teams conversations show the messages exchanged there; they don’t mirror every message from other channels. Your dot can use relevant context across those conversations. Before sharing information from a private conversation with other people, it checks that you’ve allowed it. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=context-and-memory\">Context and memory</a>.</p> <p>Open your dot's profile and select <strong>Add</strong> to see and connect the contact methods available to you. Connect apps and your computer separately to make them available for your dot’s work.</p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-and-voice\">ChatGPT and voice</h2> <p>Create, message, or call your dot in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. Mobile web is not supported.</p> <p>To call your dot, open its conversation and select the phone button. In the desktop app, you can also select <strong>Call</strong> in its profile. Talk through a request, clarify a decision, or ask for a progress update. You can type messages while you’re talking, and your dot can also message you with progress or a question. Ending a call ends the voice conversation; work you've assigned can continue. Calls initiated by your dot are planned for after launch.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: An example voice call with a dot alongside chat messages preparing a product launch review and identifying open decisions.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"slack\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack-and-teams\">Slack and Teams</h2> <p>You can message your dot in Slack and Microsoft Teams. Connect the contact method in your dot’s profile. In Slack, you can send a direct message or add your dot to a channel and mention it in a thread.</p> <p>By default, your dot responds to you in Slack. You can instruct it to engage with others. Existing permissions and safeguards still apply to what it shares and does. Your dot can message you privately to ask what you're comfortable sharing before it replies in a channel.</p> <p>Tell your dot where you want different updates. For example, keep routine progress in ChatGPT and ask it to bring decisions to you in Slack.</p> <p>For monitoring, specify which channels to check, what to watch for, and when to notify you. Ask your dot to confirm the recurring task. Adding it to a channel doesn't establish a monitoring schedule.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: An example Slack direct message and reply thread: Alex forwards a launch plan. The next morning, the dot flags a schedule risk, and Alex reviews a draft follow-up in a thread.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"ios-widgets-and-shortcuts\">iOS widgets and shortcuts</h2> <p>Open your dot from your iPhone Home Screen, or use Apple Shortcuts to choose how to start a conversation. Use the latest ChatGPT iOS app and sign in to the account where you set up your dot. These features are rolling out with ChatGPT for iOS 1.2026.279 and require <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">dot access</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"add-the-your-dot-widget\">Add the Your dot widget</h3> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The small Your dot widget with Alfred's yellow character above his name and shortcut buttons hidden.</p> </blockquote> <p>The <strong>Your dot</strong> widget shows your dot's name and appearance in a small Home Screen widget.</p> <ol> <li>Touch and hold an empty area of your Home Screen, then select <strong>Edit</strong> &gt; <strong>Add Widget</strong>.</li> <li>Find <strong>ChatGPT</strong>, choose <strong>Your dot</strong>, and select <strong>Add Widget</strong>.</li> <li>Place the widget, then select <strong>Done</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Tap your dot to open its conversation with the message composer ready. For example, open it after a meeting to add a decision to work you're already doing together.</p> <p>To add message and call controls, touch and hold the widget, select <strong>Edit Widget</strong>, and turn on <strong>Show shortcut buttons</strong>. This setting is off by default. The message button opens the composer. The phone button appears when calling is available and starts a call or returns to an active one.</p> <p>If the widget asks you to sign in or set up your dot, open ChatGPT and complete that step. Adding a widget doesn't grant dot access to an account that doesn't have it.</p> <h3 id=\"create-an-apple-shortcut\">Create an Apple shortcut</h3> <p>ChatGPT provides one <strong>Open your dot</strong> action with three <strong>Mode</strong> choices:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Mode</th> <th>What it does</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>Messaging</strong></td> <td>Opens your dot's conversation for typing a message. This is the default.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Dictation</strong></td> <td>Starts speech-to-text input for a message to your dot.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Call</strong></td> <td>Starts a live voice conversation or returns to an active call.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <ol> <li>Open Apple's <strong>Shortcuts</strong> app and create a new shortcut.</li> <li>Add an action, search for <strong>Open your dot</strong>, and select the ChatGPT action.</li> <li>Select your dot and choose a <strong>Mode</strong>.</li> <li>Name and save the shortcut, then run it to open ChatGPT in that mode.</li> </ol> <p>For example, save a shortcut named “Talk to my dot” with <strong>Call</strong> mode for a spoken progress check. Use <strong>Dictation</strong> for a quick spoken note instead. Dictation isn't available during an active call.</p> <p>On an iPhone with an Action button, open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Action Button</strong>, choose <strong>Shortcut</strong>, then <strong>Choose a Shortcut</strong> and select your saved shortcut. You can also run a saved shortcut from Apple's Shortcuts Home Screen widget.</p> <p>The action opens ChatGPT and requires authentication. If you switch accounts and a saved shortcut says the dot is no longer available, sign in to the account that owns it.</p> <h2 id=\"texting\">Texting</h2> <p>Texting is coming soon.</p>"};
